Each box weighs 15 pounds. So, the number of boxes that can be loaded is the total remaining weight (1245 pounds) divided by the weight per box (15 pounds). So, 1245 divided by 15. Let me compute that.

Dividing 1245 by 15. Well, 15 times 80 is 1200. Then 1245 - 1200 is 45. 45 divided by 15 is 3. So 80 + 3 = 83. Therefore, 15 times 83 is 1245. That seems correct.

